sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/compute-drivers.md#shared-package-cache, ADR 0207, Recall single-swamp-node + task-vms-swamp-via-ssh, docs/cli/README.md design rules R2-R4 (token minted by the Gateway, vault key names only).
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02 (second pass), rules 3 (the pinned agent's package-cache.host already validates, downloads with checked redirects, enforces the budget and writes atomically), 6 (claim, quarantine, download, verify, place and inventory are one action), 11 (one behavior per host and batch, not per artifact), 18 (batches run one at a time: the agent locks the cache), 9 and 14 (a native assert over the batch replies is the end check; no inventory read or report step), 19 (no staging cleanup: the agent removes its own temporary files), 22 (one pinned `@swamp/ssh exec` argv per batch; no curl or script steps).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · package cache fill after a lockfile change
  %% kind: task_vm.fill_package_cache
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Incus host<br/>Node 13 over ssh
  Note over GW: A lockfile changed<br/>host Node 13 · task #5182
  %%> When:
  %%> - the Gateway Git mirror sees a new default-branch commit whose lock blobs differ from the Project's snapshot
  %%> - it records the new inventory and queues one fill per configured task VM host, such as Node 13
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - Node 13 is an active, configured task VM host with a recorded SSH host key
  %%> - no other fill runs for Node 13; a second request returns the running task
  %%> - every cache key fits its 1,024-byte limit, and the inventory fits 2 batches of 4,096 archives, so the requests and replies fit the run's one terminal read
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5182 recorded with the archives, the integrity conflicts and the byte budget
  %%> - nothing has happened on Node 13 yet
  GW->>SW: Push the GitHub token<br/>task-vm-cache-fill-github-13
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - at the run start, mints a GitHub installation token with metadata read access when a Composer archive needs one
  %%> - writes only the request's `github_token` member into the Swamp vault: the token, or null
  %%> Why:
  %%> - secrets go Gateway → vault → step; the public request bytes stay in the run inputs
  %%> - serve redacts every vault value it reads with a pattern built from that value, so a vault value stays small
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-vm-cache-fill
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 13's address, user and SSH host key; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - each batch's agent request up to its `github_token` member: at most 4,096 archives, below the agent's 4 MiB request limit
  %%> - the batch numbers, the integrity conflicts, and the token's vault key name, never the token
  SW->>H: Fill the package cache<br/>ssh exec · package-cache.host
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 13 over SSH from 209 with the pinned host key
  %%> - one argv per batch: `timeout 1530 sudo -n -- orbit-agent command package-cache.host`, with the batch's request, the vault member and the closing braces on stdin
  %%> - batches run one after another; the agent holds one lock on the cache
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks each archive identity, downloads approved HTTPS URLs, checks lockfile integrity and the byte budget
  %%> - writes each verified archive and the inventory under `/var/lib/orbit/package-cache`
  %%> - skips archives that are already cached and verified, so a rerun only adds what is missing
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - per batch, the SHA-256 of each cached archive and a short public reason for each refused one
  SW->>SW: Check every archive<br/>assert
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - Swamp's native assert reads every batch reply
  %%> - it passes only when every reply is `ok`, no archive was refused, and the admission found no integrity conflict
  alt every archive is cached
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event and reads the run once; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the host inventory<br/>task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - each Project whose snapshot is unchanged gets its verified archives on Node 13
    %%> - a Project stops being pending when every host holds all its archives
    %%> - task #5182 succeeds
  else a batch or the check fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> When:
    %%> - an archive was refused or conflicts, SSH fails, or a batch exceeds its time
    Note over GW: Record what was verified<br/>task failed · next fetch retries
    %%> Result:
    %%> - archives from batch replies that arrived are recorded, so verified archives stay usable
    %%> - each refused archive is logged with its cache key and Node 13
    %%> - task #5182 fails with `task_vm.package_cache_failed`
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - verified archives stay; there is no rollback
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - the next mirror fetch queues a new fill while a Project is pending
  end
